courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon completion of this course, students are expected to

1. understand the orientation and characteristics of the Hong Kong Chinese language curriculum;
2. grasp the theories and methods of teaching various aspects of Chinese language, and apply them in teaching;
3. grasp the principles and methods of language assessment, and apply them in assessing students’ learning; ;
4. master the principles and methods of unit design, lesson design and writing of lesson plan;
5. master common language teaching strategies and techniques;
6. be able to collaborate with peers and be willing to discuss and share ideas;
7. be able to reflect on one’s practice, and to improve based on analysis.

1. Develop awareness for life-long professional growth of a mathematics teacher.

2. Understand the content and rationale behind Hong Kong primary school mathematics curriculum;
3. Construct lesson plans by selecting and sequencing “big ideas” to teach primary school mathematics;
4. Recognize different strategies, methods and techniques for teaching mathematics;
5. Use appropriate teaching resources such as physical teaching aids and computer software to teach mathematics concepts and procedures;
6. Determine prerequisite knowledge, common difficulties and effective teaching strategies for learning different mathematics topics;
7. Construct tests and other diagnosis to evaluate the effectiveness of mathematics learning and teaching;
8. Design mathematics related activities to enrich mathematics learning and teaching

Upon completion of this course, students are expected to be able to:

1. Understand the conceptual framework, aims and objectives of Primary Science, and its position in the primary curriculum;
2. Use appropriate teaching strategies and methods for Primary Science;
3. Design and implement multiple-approach of assessment for Primary Science;
4. Deliver Primary Science lessons effectively;
5. Possess the awareness to be reflective for future professional development.

